\subsection{State and Error Convention}
\label{sec:state}

The nominal quaternion is stored separately from the additive navigation and
bias states.  For $q\in\Sph^3$,
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:nominal-state-vector}
\vct{x}_{\mathrm{nom}} =
\begin{bmatrix}
q &
\vct{b}_g^{\top} &
\vct{v}^{\top} &
\vct{p}^{\top} &
\vct{S}^{\top} &
\vct{a}_w^{\top} &
\vct{b}_a^{\top}
\end{bmatrix}^{\!\top}.
\end{equation}
The quaternion is propagated and corrected on $\Sph^3$.

The covariance is defined for the local error state
\begin{equation}
\label{eq:state-vector}
\delta\vct{x} =
\begin{bmatrix}
\delta\vct{\theta}^{\top} &
\delta\vct{b}_g^{\top} &
\delta\vct{v}^{\top} &
\delta\vct{p}^{\top} &
\delta\vct{S}^{\top} &
\delta\vct{a}_w^{\top} &
\delta\vct{b}_a^{\top}
\end{bmatrix}^{\!\top},
\end{equation}
with left-multiplicative attitude error $\delta\vct\theta$
\cite{Shuster1993_AttitudeRepresentations,MarkleyCrassidis2014_Attitude}.
The world-NED quantities $\vct v$, $\vct p$, and
$\vct S=\int\vct p\,dt$ denote velocity, oscillatory displacement, and its
integral; $\vct a_w$ is latent OU acceleration. Gyroscope bias $\vct b_g$
is a random walk, and $\vct b_a$ is a slow OU residual about the calibrated
temperature curve. With both bias blocks enabled, the covariance
$\mat P=\E[\delta\vct x\delta\vct x^\top]$ has dimension $N_X=21$.

Two acceleration covariances must be distinguished.
$\matg{\Sigma}_{aw}^{\mathrm{stat}}$ is the prescribed stationary covariance
of the OU prior and determines $\matg{Q}_d$, whereas $\mat{P}_{a_wa_w}$ is the
posterior uncertainty of the estimated acceleration state.  Changing
$\matg{\Sigma}_{aw}^{\mathrm{stat}}$ does not overwrite
$\mat{P}_{a_wa_w}$.  Hard initialization may reset this posterior block and its
cross-covariances; default online maintenance only adds the positive-semidefinite
covariance required to reach the current stationary floor.

